{"dossier":"D03","entry_points":[{"sids":["kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lc_start","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lc_next","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lc_stop","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lockdep_chains_ops"],"text":"Chain report walks stored chains in order; start yields header, negatives fail, later slots map via next-valid helper, stop idles, ops table wires callbacks."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lockdep_stats_debug_show","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lockdep_stats_show","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lockdep_proc_init"],"text":"Stats reporter tallies safe/unsafe use across irq contexts plus classes, chains and stack; debug adds lookup/cycle counts. Init exposes chain, stats and writable detail files."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_0","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_1","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_2","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::ww_acquire_ctxs","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_init","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_exit","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_unlock"],"text":"Ww torture owns three mutexes plus per-writer contexts; init builds shared class and allocates array with OOM alert, exit frees, release unwraps all then finalizes slot."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_init","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_cleanup","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_writer","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_reader"],"text":"Init picks ops by name, defaults threads from online CPUs, starts interleaved workers plus reporter with shared teardown. Workers loop acquire, hold, release under stutter."}],"exports":[{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_spin_lock_write_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_spin_lock_write_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_spin_lock_write_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_spin_lock_write_unlock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::raw_spin_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::raw_spin_lock_irq_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_lock_busted_write_lock"],"text":"Raw spin torture offers write-only plain and irq-saving ops; both always succeed, irq form saves state centrally for restore, shared hooks stay empty with label."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/mutex.c::ww_mutex_lock.alt_1","kernel/locking/mutex.c::ww_mutex_lock.alt_2","kernel/locking/mutex.c::__ww_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/mutex.c::__ww_mutex_lock_slowpath","kernel/locking/ww_rt_mutex.c::ww_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/ww_rt_mutex.c::__ww_rt_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwsem_down_write","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwsem_write_delay","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwsem_up_write","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwsem_down_read","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::down_write","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::down_read","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::up_write"],"text":"Ww and rwsem acquisition sleep; ww tries nonblocking then slow path with deadlock check, rwsem torture adds dwell, core down/up pair dep tracking with contended helpers."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_down_write","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_up_write","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_free_rwsem","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_percpu_rwsem_down_write","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_percpu_rwsem_up_write","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_percpu_rwsem_down_read","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_percpu_rwsem_up_read"],"text":"Percpu rwsem exposes writer acquire, release and reclaim; torture shims forward both directions, ignore thread id and treat acquire as infallible."}],"extracts":["55b1a27955da90fce5a21e07229789ba6dfd032847d03720cc6d597987722bd0","6a02ed428306172949958ef34ea413767063db045cfd8e917597fdf5fb209ac8","761f237601f6a6fb38479966e5839fbf0bb01921659c455c7bafe4c436ff43ae"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_lock_busted_write_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_lock_busted_write_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_busted_ops","kernel/locking/mutex.c::ww_mutex_deadlock_injection","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_spin_lock_write_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_spin_lock_write_unlock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_res_spin_write_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_write_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_read_lock_irq"],"text":"Busted ops succeed without exclusion, baseline only. Deadlock injection fires on countdown to test wound path, inert when off. Irq forms share one flag slot; overlap would clobber."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rt_boost_rtmutex","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rtmutex_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rtmutex_delay","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rtmutex_unlock"],"text":"RT boost and long holds stay inert unless flags enable them. RT dwell mixes brief pauses, rare extended holds and occasional yields scaled by writer count."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_free_rwsem","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::__percpu_down_read_trylock","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::readers_active_check","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_down_write","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_rwsem_wait","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_stats_print"],"text":"Free tolerates empty object and nulls pointer. Tally updates need preempt control with pairing fences. Writer and waiter paths sleep uninterruptibly. Stats print skips on alloc fail."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::MAX_NESTED_LOCKS","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::seq_header","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lockdep_proc_init","kernel/locking/mcs_spinlock.h::arch_mcs_spin_lock_contended","kernel/locking/mcs_spinlock.h::arch_mcs_spin_unlock_contended","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::rwsem_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::percpu_rwsem_lock_ops"],"text":"Nesting cap eight; detail version 0.4; files lockdep, lockdep_chains, lockdep_stats, lock_stat. MCS unlock stores one with release, lock spins for it. Tables carry rwsem and percpu names."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lc_show","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lockdep_stats_show","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lock_stat_cmp","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::seq_line","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::snprint_time","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::seq_time","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::seq_lock_time","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::seq_stats","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::seq_header"],"text":"Chains show irq label plus keyed levels; header flags exhaustion. Only used classes count; order ranks waits first, durations scaled, sections conditional. Names read under sched RCU."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_type","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::bind_readers","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::bind_writers","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::stats_task","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::writer_tasks","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::reader_tasks","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_is_write_held","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_is_read_held","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::last_lock_release","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::cxt","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::param_set_cpumask","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::param_get_cpumask","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::cpumask_nonempty","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lt_bind_ops"],"text":"Default is rt-safe spin under PREEMPT_RT else spin. Globals track workers, held flags and release time; context starts empty. Binding parses list, warns and resets to all on failure."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_lock_busted_write_delay","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_spin_lock_write_delay","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwsem_read_delay","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_writer","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_reader","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::__torture_print_stats","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_stats_print","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_stats","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_print_module_parms"],"text":"Holds mix rare long waits, brief pauses and rare yields scaled by workers. Held-flag overlap counts as failure. Reports aggregate totals and extremes; config is logged once."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_mutex_nested_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_mutex_nested_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rtmutex_nested_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rtmutex_nested_unlock","kernel/locking/ww_rt_mutex.c::__ww_rt_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/rtmutex_api.c::rt_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::rwsem_clear_owner","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::rwsem_owner"],"text":"Nested helpers scan bitmask up to acquire, down to release. RT ww rejects same-context rebind and tries before sleeping. Owner packs task plus flags; clear requires no preempt."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::per_cpu_sum","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::readers_active_check","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_up_write","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_down_write","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::pcpu_rwsem","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_percpu_rwsem_init","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_percpu_rwsem_exit","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::percpu_rwsem_lock_ops"],"text":"Writer moves announced to contention to draining to held; release clears marker, wakes one, exits regime after grace. Quiescence sums CPU tallies; one static object is stressed."}],"locks":[{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_spinlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_spin_lock_write_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_spin_lock_write_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::spin_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_spin_lock_write_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_lock_spin_write_unlock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::rqspinlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_res_spin_write_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_res_spin_write_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::raw_res_spin_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_res_spin_write_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_raw_res_spin_write_unlock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::raw_res_spin_lock_irq_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_mutex_unlock","kernel/locking/rtmutex_api.c::__rt_mutex_init","kernel/locking/rtmutex_api.c::__rt_mutex_lock_common","kernel/locking/rtmutex_api.c::rt_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/rtmutex_api.c::rt_mutex_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rtmutex_lock"],"text":"Spin, resilient, mutex and rtmutex torture use one global each; irq forms save state centrally. Rt acquire registers dep state first, release withdraws before unlock."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/mutex.c::ww_mutex_unlock","kernel/locking/ww_mutex.h::__ww_mutex_unlock","kernel/locking/ww_rt_mutex.c::ww_mutex_unlock","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::__up_write.alt_1","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::rwsem_clear_owner","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::rwsem_owner","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::up_write"],"text":"Ww release detaches context, decrements held count, then unlocks base; rt differs in dep tracking. Rwsem release checks owner, clears without preempt, drops count, wakes if flagged."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::__percpu_down_write_trylock","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_down_write","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::__percpu_down_read_trylock","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::__percpu_rwsem_trylock","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_rwsem_wait","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwsem_up_read"],"text":"Writers contend one atomic marker. Readers bump CPU tally, fence, sample marker; on set they undo and prod waiter. Waiters queue under spinlock with irqs off and sleep uninterruptibly."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F4"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lock_stat_open","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::ls_start","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::ls_next","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::ls_stop","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::ls_show","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lockstat_ops","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lock_stat_write","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lock_stat_release","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lock_stat_proc_ops"],"text":"Detail flow snapshots and sorts active classes, emits header then one record each; leading-zero input clears stats, release frees buffer; seq and file ops wire it."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::__torture_rt_boost","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rt_boost","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_write_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_write_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_read_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_read_unlock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_write_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_write_unlock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_read_lock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_read_unlock_irq","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_write_delay","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_rwlock_read_delay"],"text":"Boost idles unless enabled, else elevates workers at random intervals then restores. Rwlock gives symmetric exclusive/shared plus irq twins with central stash and scaled dwell."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_lock","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::torture_ww_mutex_0","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::__up_write.alt_2","kernel/locking/rwbase_rt.c::rwbase_write_unlock","kernel/locking/rwbase_rt.c::__rwbase_write_unlock","kernel/locking/rwsem.c::rwbase_rtmutex_unlock","kernel/locking/spinlock_rt.c::rwbase_rtmutex_unlock"],"text":"Ww acquire builds ordered triple, walks it, unwinds predecessors on failure, slow-paths and reorders on deadlock. RT rwsem release serializes, adjusts readers, unlocks base."}],"structs":[{"sids":["kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lock_stat_data","kernel/locking/lockdep_proc.c::lock_stat_seq"],"text":"Snapshot pairs class pointer with counter copy; table sized by key limit with end marker bounding the populated prefix for walk and sort."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::rw_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::rw_lock_irq_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::mutex_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::ww_mutex_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::rtmutex_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::rwsem_lock_ops","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::percpu_rwsem_lock_ops"],"text":"Tables hold exclusive acquire, dwell, boost, release plus optional shared hooks, lifecycle and nested hooks, irq state and name; rw populates shared, others leave empty."},{"sids":["kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_torture_cxt","kernel/locking/locktorture.c::lock_stress_stats","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_free_rwsem","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_down_write","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_up_write","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::percpu_rwsem_wait","kernel/locking/percpu-rwsem.c::__percpu_down_read_trylock"],"text":"Context holds worker counts, flags, error tally, active ops and per-role stats. Percpu state holds tallies, regime sync, marker, wait object, queue and dep map."}],"stubs":[]}
